# .env.client — the CLIENT-FACING config (the I-10 recorded sample / a live
# demo link). NOT the dev default. See D-13 (STT), D-15 (TTS), D-20 (dialogue)
# in the engagement decision log.
#
# The dev defaults (local Whisper, gemma4:cloud, premade voices) are for
# building — they are free but slow and unpredictable (gemma4:cloud on the
# Ollama free tier: 13–86 s per turn). The client hears a different stack:
# dedicated infra, ~2–5 s per turn, and the Ukrainian library voices.
#
# Usage: copy your working .env, then apply the three flips below.
# Prereqs: prepay OpenAI ($5 — one key covers whisper-1 + gpt-4.1-mini),
#          add gpt-4.1-mini to the project's Allowed models + verify the org
#          (gpt-4.1-mini is a "protected model"); upgrade ElevenLabs to
#          Starter ($6 — unlocks the library voices).

# --- 1. STT: local Whisper (~12 s/turn, CPU) → whisper-1 (~2–4 s) ---
STT_BACKEND=openai
# WHISPER_LANG still applies as the language hint

# --- 2. dialogue: gemma4:cloud (free, queue tail) → gpt-4.1-mini (dedicated) ---
# gpt-4.1-mini, not gpt-4o-mini: 4o-mini asked the client to pick a
# certification level and guessed past the KB (2026-09-03). ~2.7x the token
# price, still cents for the demo.
DIALOG_BACKEND=openai
DIALOG_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini

# --- 3. TTS: premade Sarah/George → the Ukrainian library voices ---
TTS_BACKEND=elevenlabs
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_A=2OXYbN1uGomXXJtv9Dq6
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_B=4nLP0u2B3yI0lyzATFnN

# --- the one key both #1 and #2 need (must have a positive balance) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Everything else (TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, KB/prompt paths,
# DATA_DIR) is unchanged from your dev .env. BOT_TIMEZONE defaults to
# Europe/Kyiv — set it explicitly if the demo host runs on UTC, otherwise the
# "within 15 minutes / next business morning" line will use the wrong clock.
#
# Before recording: run docs/smoke-test.md §2 / §6 / §7 / §13 on THIS config
# (§13 = voice — the thing the client actually judges). §2 is being swept on
# the client stack now (2026-09-03); §6 / §7 / §13 still pending.
